  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1242 PM CDT Sat Sep 26 2026\n\nTuesday through Saturday:\n\nAs the ridge heads eastward Tuesday, the door will open for a \nreturn of deeper moisture into southern Wisconsin. Precipitable \nwater values are currently expected to increase to around 1.5\" \nby later Tuesday into Tuesday night. A shortwave moving through \nlate in the day or overnight will then bring a return of shower \nchances to the forecast area. A few rumbles of thunder will be \npossible as well, though instability is still looking minimal.\n\nModels remain mixed with precip chances for the latter half of \nnext week, depending on how far south the deeper moisture gets \npushed after the Tue/Tue night system rolls through. There is \nthe potential for quick moisture return late in the week along \nwith more shower chances per the latest GFS and Canadian\nsolutions. The ECMWF is faster with the arrival of the surface\nhigh, keeping the frontal boundary and moisture to the south of\nthe state line through late week. Confidence thus remains on \nthe lower end for precip chances late in the week.\n\nTemperatures are expected to remain within a couple degrees of\nnormal through the extended forecast period.\n\nDDV",
